{title: Why Have You Forsaken Me}
{subtitle: Psalms 22:1–2}
{key: C}
{tempo: 70}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [C] | [C] | [G/B] | [Am7] |
| [Fmaj7] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
My [C]God my [G]God [Fmaj7]why have you forsaken me
[C]Why so [G]far from saving [Fmaj7]me
So [C]far from the [G/B]words of my groan[Am]ing
I call by [Fmaj7]day and you do not an[G]swer
By [Dm7]night I find no [F]rest
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Yet you are [C]holy
[G]Enthroned on the praises [Am7]of Israel [Fmaj7]
You are [C]holy
Ent[G]hroned on the praises [Am7]of Israel [F]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]In you [G]our [Am]fathers trusted
They [F]trusted and you [G]rescued [C]them
My God my [G]God [Am]why have you forsaken me
[C]Why so [G]far from saving [F]me
So [C]far from the [G]words of my groan[Am]ing
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Yet [Dm7]you are ho[F]ly [C]
[G]Enthroned on the praises [Am7]of Israel [F]
You are ho[C]ly
[G]Enthroned on the praises [Am7]of Israel [F]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
My [C]God my [G]God
[Am]Why have you forsaken me [F][C]
{end_of_verse}
